"""kernels/muse_decode_layer/measure_t1_v1.py (C37, MEASUREMENT-ONLY, generated by tools/gen_measure_t1_v1.py): the T = 1 quick-win study of Argon's corridor ideas.

No GPU:  file rules, kernel_fn / prepare are sonnet_v5f verbatim, in sync with the generator, the derived `_t1_kernel` differs from v5f's `_kernel_sglang` in exactly four marked hunks,
         the patched small-M device source differs from v5f's in exactly three, the facts the claim verdicts rest on (SMALLM_CFG row, pdl_trigger before the K-loop, 16 staged rows, ps1
         from T = 2), variant switches / winners / combo / report (<= 14 KB, S lines first) with a stubbed environment.
Dev GPU (RTX 2060, sm_75, NVRTC, no SGLang): the patched kernels (nz1 8, 8 rows, trig_late) BITWISE v5f's at M = 1 and 16, the route on a side stream inside a two-stream CUDA graph, sm_90
         assembly of the patched source (regs / spills / the trigger's place in the PTX), the timing machinery on a toy callable; LAST: the router-fix kernel's smem for sm_90a (claim A2).
Run:     tools/heavy.sh .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_measure_t1_v1.py   (with set -o pipefail)"""
